- Story & Context: Elias stood at the intersection of Blackwood and Fourth, watching the traffic signals blink in a syncopated sequence he’d spent months coding. The smell of ozone filled the air as the streetlights began to strobe, a sensory overload that triggered the city-wide blackout. "You move when the wire tells you to," he muttered, watching the first note of the piano ripple through the static of the grid.
